      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Danny Rivers was convicted in Texas state court of continuous sexual abuse of a child and related charges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Matthew Guarnieri argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae urging affrmance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court denied Rivers's habeas petition, issuing its judgment in September 2018."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rivers",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rivers argues that this fling did not qualify as a second or successive application triggering \u00a7 2244(b) because it was submitted during the pendency of his appeal of the judgment related to his frst habeas petition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not agree with that proposition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our case law establishes instead that whether a fling qualifes as a second or successive application generally turns on the existence of a fnal judgment with respect to the frst petition, not the status of an appeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thus, they are not themselves properly considered to be second or successive flings under AEDPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A second-in-time \u00a7 2254 petition generally qualifes as a second or successive application, triggering the requirements of \u00a7 2244(b), when an earlier fled petition has been decided on the merits and a judgment exists."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
